<title>RUSSIA: TABLE-Russia Q1 debt servicing falls to $1.4 bln.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Russia Q1 debt servicing falls to $1.4 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia spent $1.4 billion on servicing its foreign debt in the first quarter of this year against $2.4 billion in the same period of 1996, the central bank said in its bulletin.</p>
<p>The actual figure due in debt servicing fell to $3.6 billion in the first quarter of 1997 from $5.7 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following figures:</p>
<p>    billions of dollars		  Q1 1997   Q4 1996  Q1 1996</p>
<p>    payments due				3.6	 3.6	5.7</p>
<p>    actual payments			   1.4	 1.7	2.4</p>
<p>debt service ratio (exports) pct:</p>
<p>    payments due			     15.2	12.9     24.0</p>
<p>    actual payments			   6.0	 6.2     10.0</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
<p>e-mail: moscow.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
